Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: dedicated editorial blog hero for Praderas, accompanying an article about OpenTerminalUI v2.3 and why adding more market information is not the same as making sense of it. Scene: a calm wooden research desk beside an open window overlooking a green meadow in soft late-afternoon natural light. Main visual metaphor: one elegant magnifying lens bringing a deliberately chosen small cluster of paper cards into clear focus, with other loose papers remaining softly out of focus around them. The selected cards have only abstract shapes suggesting a price line, a news page and a calendar, absolutely no readable text or numbers. Style: sophisticated quiet cinematic editorial illustration, tactile paper and wood, restrained sage green, warm amber and neutral cream, professional and thoughtful, not a stock photo or neon cyberpunk. Composition: wide landscape hero, one clear focal mass, important content within central 70 percent so it also works in a 1200x630 social crop and small thumbnail. No people, robots, brains, causal arrows, readable text, logos, brand marks or watermarks. Opaque background.
